  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DCM B3T2 BT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IFC is considering an investment of up to EUR100&#xa0;million in a privately placed subordinated bond CRR compliant&#xa0; (B3T2) of Banca Transilvania S.A. (BT or the Bank), the largest bank in Romania and IFCs long-time partner, which will be listed on the Bucharest Stock Exchange (the Bond). The Bond will undergo closed subscription and be subscribed by IFC and investors mobilized by IFC. The IFC use of proceeds is residential mortgages, with at least 80% earmarked to green mortgages (the Project).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Projects development impact is achieved by:
(i)increasing access to housing finance, by supporting a leading bank to grow its mortgage portfolio;
(ii)supporting households in building or purchasing properties in green-certified buildings; 
(iii)supporting a sustainable mortgage market, by catalyzing the adoption of green mortgage lending standards, through demonstration and replication channels.</narrative>
  </description>
